6.2 Scheduling

Goal: Select the maximum number of non-overlapping events.

❌ Shortest event first → wrong
❌ Earliest starting time → wrong
✅ Earliest ending time → correct
Sort events by end time.
Greedily take an event if start >= last_end.

Pattern:

Maximize number of non-overlapping intervals → sort by ending time.

6.3 Tasks & Deadlines

Goal: Maximize total score where each task gives deadline - finish_time.

Deadlines don't affect the optimal ordering.
✅ Sort tasks by duration ascending.
Reason: swapping a longer task before a shorter one always improves the total score.

Pattern:

Minimize total completion time → Shortest Job First.

6.4 Minimizing Sums

Given:

Σ |ai - x|^c

c = 1
Σ |ai - x|
✅ Optimal x = median
Sort → choose middle.
If n is even, any x between the two middle values works.

Remember:

Absolute distance → Median

c = 2
Σ (ai - x)²
✅ Optimal x = average / mean

Remember:

Squared distance → Mean

